      "id": "be-s12m-monopoly-c1",
      "heading": "The monopoly environment and its sources",
      "explanation_md": "- A **single firm serves the relevant market**; most monopolies are **local**.\n- The firm's demand **is the market demand curve**.\n- The firm **controls price**, but price affects how much it sells.\n\n| Natural sources | Created sources |\n|---|---|\n| Economies of scale | Patents and other legal barriers (like licenses) |\n| Economies of scope | Tying contracts |\n| Cost complementarities | Exclusive contracts |",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Natural: scale, scope, cost complementarities. Created: patents and licenses, tying contracts, exclusive contracts.",
      "clarification": null,
