    {
      "id": "be-s12m-monopoly-c2",
      "heading": "Marginal revenue and profit maximization",
      "explanation_md": "Market power lets you **price above MC**, but the sky is not the limit: **how much you sell depends on the price you set**.\n\n- MR lies **below demand**. Where demand is **elastic**, MR > 0 and TR rises; at **unit elastic**, MR = 0 and TR peaks; where **inelastic**, MR < 0.\n- **Produce where MR = MC**, then **charge the price on the demand curve** for that quantity.\n- **Profit = (P - ATC) x Q**.\n\n**Useful formulae:** for linear demand **P = a - bQ**, **MR = a - 2bQ**. Alternatively **MR = P[(1 + E) / E]**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "MR = MC for quantity, demand curve for price. Linear demand P = a - bQ gives MR = a - 2bQ.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
        {
          "id": "be-s12m-monopoly-q-581e32c5",
          "type": "mcq",
          "stem": "If P = a - bQ, then MR is:",
          "options": [
