    {
      "id": "be-s12m-monopoly-c4",
      "heading": "Long run, deadweight loss and the case for monopoly",
      "explanation_md": "**Long run:** no adjustment, **unless the source of monopoly power is eliminated**.\n\n**Why government dislikes monopoly:** **P > MC**, so there is **too little output at too high a price**, creating a **deadweight loss of monopoly**.\n\n**Arguments for monopoly:** economies of scale, economies of scope and cost complementarities **may outweigh** the harm from market power, and monopoly **encourages innovation**.\n\n**Multi-plant decisions:** a monopoly with two plants sets **MR(Q) = MC1(Q1) = MC2(Q2)** and charges **P(Q)** where **Q = Q1 + Q2**.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-electricity-two-plants"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Monopoly: P > MC, too little output, deadweight loss. Two plants: MR = MC1 = MC2.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
